# Completion review: generic compatible model metadata (2026-10-29)

## Scope and implementation

- Added one shared metadata parser, per-provider/connection current snapshot, and
  normalized persistence path for stored `openai-compatible` and
  `anthropic-compatible` nodes. Removed the APInex-specific collector, hook,
  and namespace without a compatibility reader.
- Reused the native route's protocol shapes, auth roles, outbound guards, and
  proxy resolution. The periodic models.dev lifecycle refreshes active
  compatible connections independently; one endpoint failure does not block
  models.dev pricing/capability writes. Credential resolution uses the native
  lazy-decrypt getter.
- Added one same-origin configured endpoint builder for validation and
  discovery. OpenAI default probes and both protocols' existing relative path
  behavior remain; configured endpoint errors do not fall back. Anthropic
  snapshots replace only after complete pagination.
- The same builder validates the `modelsPath` field on provider-node
  create/update and the provider-node validation endpoint. The existing field
  still accepts slash-prefixed paths and now accepts same-origin HTTP(S) URLs;
  cross-origin endpoints are rejected before a request.
- Stores current source URL without query/fragment, original fetch timestamp,
  exact raw IDs, normalized display name/limits/selected capabilities, and only
  explicit finite non-negative per-million prices. Duplicate IDs are omitted
  fail-closed. Failed/incomplete refresh keeps the prior source record and age.
- Compatible pricing and strict-zero evidence bind to exact synced raw IDs and
  current eligible provider connections. Conflicting, unknown, stale, and
  future prices fail closed. Explicit compatible false capabilities from an
  active eligible connection beat canonical defaults; inactive/excluded
  connections do not contribute, and operator/provider overrides retain
  precedence.
- Integrated review caught a duplicate-ID case that could preserve prior zero
  metadata and a design statement that overstated catalog/snapshot atomicity.
  Duplicate raw IDs are now omitted from the replacement, and the design records
  the existing sequential catalog write followed by one snapshot upsert.
  Create/update schema and validation coverage was also extended after source
  audit found the existing absolute endpoint was rejected before discovery.
- The superseded APInex spec now contains only removed/superseded deltas; a
  duplicate active-looking freshness block was deleted while historical
  completion receipts remain intact.
- The Anthropic fixture and field mapping follow the official documented
  `image_input.supported`, `display_name`, token-limit, and pagination fields.
  `server_tools` is not inferred as caller tool-use support. See [Anthropic
  List Models](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/models/list) and [OpenAI
  List Models](https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/models/methods/list).

## Verification

- Focused compatible metadata, discovery, capability, endpoint schema,
  models.dev pricing, and benchmark-hook tests: **89/89 passed**. The existing
  models.dev live-API test
  performs a public models.dev catalog GET; compatible provider fetches use
  test fixtures/mocks.
- Focused ESLint on changed production modules and new focused test files
  passed. Full changed-file ESLint remains red on 11 pre-existing diagnostics:
  nine unused imports/types in the route and two `any` annotations in the
  extended test file; none is an added line in this change.
- Prettier passed for the changed code and OpenSpec files except
  `src/app/api/provider-nodes/[id]/route.ts`; its clean-base source also fails
  Prettier. Existing unrelated formatting was left untouched, and the added
  lines follow the project formatter. `git diff --check` passed. Strict
  OpenSpec validation passed for this package and both superseded APInex
  packages.
- `npm run typecheck:core -- --pretty false` remains nonzero with **720**
  diagnostics, exactly matching the clean-base diagnostic set; no diagnostic
  names a changed production module. This is not a passing typecheck.
- Code Simplifier was applied to the changed source. The pass removed an
  unsupported Anthropic `tool_use` inference after primary-doc verification and
  normalized configured URL whitespace at one boundary. No other simplification
  preserved the selected protocol/auth and exact-identity behavior more clearly.

## Review and release boundary

- Fresh independent integrated review returned no actionable findings. The
  reviewer ran no tests or builds.
- Local commit is the end of this package. GitHub build/release, deployment,
  provider requests/completions, and native free-only acceptance remain
  separate open gates in `openspec/TODO.md`. This change does not archive or
  claim release acceptance. No runtime state or credentials were changed or
  exposed.

## Merged-runtime import correction — 2026-10-29

- GitHub ARM64 run `40954554580` failed its actual emitted-module check with
  Node exit 13 and unsettled top-level await while importing
  `modelBenchmarkSearch-Y5TC2YLC.mjs`. The source graph on main `0c316b9`
  showed a new cycle from `modelsDevSync` through compatible discovery,
  validation URL helpers, Claude runtime/context management, and capability
  resolution back to `modelsDevSync`.
- Moved the pure compatible endpoint and suffix helpers into
  `src/shared/utils/compatibleProviderUrls.ts`. Validation and discovery use
  that module directly; Claude service and its callers use the same helper.
  No compatibility exports remain. `--check-runtime`, its operator, and
  Dockerfile are unchanged.
- `tests/unit/compatibleModelImportGraph.test.mjs` traverses static TypeScript
  imports with the repository resolver. It passes on this source and fails on
  clean base `0c316b9` because `src/lib/providers/validation/urlHelpers.ts`
  is reachable from compatible discovery. The test verifies that the operator
  source's `--check-runtime` branch follows the awaited benchmark-module import
  and exits only after that import. It does not prove generated-artifact
  behavior; the GitHub runtime check remains authoritative.
- Focused compatible metadata, discovery, capability, endpoint-schema,
  models.dev pricing, Claude helper/request, and benchmark-hook suite: **109/109
  passed**. The import graph test passes **2/2**. Compatible provider requests
  use mocks; the pre-existing models.dev test makes its public catalog GET.
- Code Simplifier reviewed the moved helper boundary and regression. It sorted
  the changed import groups and reduced the graph test to TypeScript's existing
  module resolver/preprocessor; no further safe simplification remained.
- Core TypeScript check remains red with **720 diagnostics**. A clean worktree
  at base `0c316b9`, using the same dependencies and command, has the identical
  720 diagnostics: **0 added, 0 removed**, and no diagnostics in changed source
  modules. Focused ESLint passes for changed production files and the graph
  test. Including two existing Claude test files reports 29 `no-explicit-any`
  errors at untouched lines. Prettier and `git diff --check` pass; strict
  OpenSpec validation reports this change valid.
- A separate pre-existing source path reaches usage migrations:
  `src/lib/modelBenchmarkSearch.ts` → `src/lib/search/executeWebSearch.ts` →
  `open-sse/handlers/search.ts` → `src/lib/usageDb.ts` →
  `src/lib/usage/migrations.ts`. The last module invokes migration/archive
  work at import time under its existing disk-persistence condition. GitHub
  logs show SQLite initialization but do not isolate which call opens it. This
  path was unchanged; this correction does not claim `--check-runtime` is
  side-effect-free.
- Fresh independent review found a P2 because the first operator assertion
  only matched an awaited import and overstated emitted-artifact coverage. The
  final test checks the flag, import-before-branch ordering, and success exit
  after import; documentation now leaves artifact proof to GitHub. The reviewer
  rechecked and confirmed resolution with no remaining actionable findings.
- No local app/image/bundle build or provider request was made. The generated
  ARM64 artifact check remains open and requires a separately authorized
  GitHub run. Deployment, provider acceptance, and native free-only completion
  remain open; do not archive this package.
